Redis - 
Redis as a Cache
Redis as a Distributed Lock
- one issue , primary dies after acquiring lock and replication stop and , replica becomes primary  ,
  another acquires lock now two holder acquire same lock and do the transaction

- solve it by fencing tokens - token given by redis on each lock acquires 
example - 

t=0   Client A acquires lock, gets token 100
      Client A starts doing work...

t=15  Client A pauses (GC freeze, OS scheduling)
      Lock TTL expires

t=16  Client B acquires lock, gets token 101
      Client B does work, writes to storage with token 101 ✅
      Storage records: "last seen token = 101"

t=45  Client A resumes, still thinks it holds the lock
      Client A tries to write to storage with token 100
      Storage checks: 100 < 101 → REJECT ❌





